  "hindi": "हम घी का नाम प्रकट करें; इस यज्ञ में नमस्कारों के साथ धारण करें। ब्रह्मा पास आकर सुने जो पढ़ा जा रहा है; चार सींगों वाले गौर ने यह उँडेला है।",
  "english": "Let us proclaim the name of ghee; in this sacrifice let us uphold with homages. Let the Brahman priest listen to what is being recited; the four-horned pale one has poured this out.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "dhārayāmā has no stated object. avamīt read as the aorist of ava-√vam ('poured out, discharged'); form uncertain. gaura 'pale, whitish' rendered literally; it might denote an animal (bison) but the verse does not say. upa śṛṇavat: upa-√śru 'listen to'. brahmā taken as the Brahman priest (not brahman, n.).",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
