  "hindi": "ये सौ धाराओं वाली, हृदय से सम्बन्धित समुद्र से बहती हैं, जिन्हें कपटी देख नहीं सकता। मैं घी की धाराओं को देखता हूँ; इनके बीच एक सुनहरा बेंत है।",
  "english": "These flow from the sea of the heart, with a hundred courses, not to be seen by a deceiver. I gaze at the streams of ghee; in the midst of these is a golden reed.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "hṛdyāt samudrāt: hṛdya is an adjective 'of the heart', rendered 'the sea of the heart'. śatavrajāḥ 'with a hundred courses' (vraja 'pen, course'). ripuṇā na avacakṣe: 'not to be seen by a deceiver' (ripu also 'enemy'); the infinitive is read passively. vetasaḥ 'reed' is a literal gloss. 'is' in the last clause is not in the Sanskrit.",
